<h1>Release notes for version 1.4.9</h1>
<h2>Inspector, Agent, and Native Describe</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Add shared inspector tabs so resource details, native describe output, and Krust Agent can live in the same inspector without reparenting the main table.</li>
  <li>Keep the Agent conversation shared across resource views while restoring model selection, new chat, and prompt suggestions in compact inspector mode.</li>
  <li>Add native describe access for pods and keep large describe output on the existing SwiftUI renderer with scroll behavior that matches other inspectors.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Resource Visibility and Metrics</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Add Prometheus-backed CPU and memory charts to pod and workload inspectors when a verified Prometheus service is configured.</li>
  <li>Improve pod, workload, storage, networking, configuration, and access-control inspectors with cache-first data, colored labels, compact chips, and better scanability.</li>
  <li>Add pod exec entry points from the pod inspector so common shell access is available without opening the row context menu first.</li>
</ul>
<h2>RBAC, CRDs, Helm, and k9r</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Expand RBAC topology so subjects, bindings, roles, rules, and workload usage are easier to trace visually.</li>
  <li>Improve CRD, native describe, Helm, logs, and local routing workflows for large clusters and long values.</li>
  <li>Continue k9r parity work with more Kubernetes resource actions, keyboard flows, and shared Rust-core behavior.</li>
</ul>
</body></html>
